# Core Development Workflow

## Split Views & Comparisons
- Enable split views by default for file comparisons
- Make it trivial to open two files side-by-side
- Use diff previews before applying changes
- Keep changes small and reviewable

## Project Structure
- Assume `src/` layout for Python projects
- Respect [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml) as the single source of truth
- Reference [Makefile](mdc:Makefile) for build/QA targets

## Code Quality
- Always show a one-screen diff for each AI edit
- Explain why changes are made, not just what
- Prefer structured, reviewable changes over large refactors
- Use British English in comments, docs, commit messages, and PR text